{
  "protocol": "at",
  "version": "1.2",
  "notes": "Plain text must be the entire body (one trailing newline allowed). JSON name may omit @. Length is 1 to 15 characters, mixed in any order: letters, [0-9_], one Extended_Pictographic scalar, a flag pair counted as one character, a ZWJ sequence counted as one character, one non-ASCII currency sign, or one non-ASCII number. @Ðoge is a handle and is not @doge. @犬jon, @jo犬n, and @jon犬 are handles. @👨‍💻 is one character and is not @👨. The pirate flag is one character and is not @🏴. A skin-tone emoji, a keycap, and a subdivision flag are one character each. @👍🏽 is not @👍. @0⃣ is not @0. @🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿 is not @🏴. A lone regional indicator, a stray ZWJ, or a combining mark is not a handle. A lookalike is a different handle, not a rejected one. A dot, a DNS marker, or a DX marker never registers a handle. v1.2 does not change any v1.1 canonical handle. v1.1: content type is never consulted; p is compared ASCII case-insensitively and must be 'at' (p:'@' is not a marker); a duplicated JSON key takes its last value.",
